      en: "Czersk Castle, located 30 km south of Warsaw, was built in the 14th century by Duke Janusz I of Warsaw. It served as a residence for Masovian dukes and a key defensive point along the Vistula River. The Gothic brick castle underwent several modifications and was destroyed during the Swedish wars in the 17th century. Today it stands as a picturesque ruin surrounded by a deep moat. The restored towers offer panoramic views of the surrounding landscape and the nearby town of Czersk, founded in the 13th century.",
