      en: "Cieszyn Castle Hill (Czech: Těšín) is the historic core of the town, featuring a Piast castle from the 10th century. The castle was the seat of the Duchy of Teschen and expanded in the 13th century. Only the Rotunda of St. Nicholas (from the 11th century) and the Piast Tower survive from the original complex. The hill offers panoramic views of the city and the Olza River. The castle was abandoned in the 18th century and fell into ruin. Today it is an archaeological monument and tourist attraction.",
